 "problems": [
  "Bash/curl egress to clerk.house.gov is blocked by the proxy. Every roll call was read through the WebFetch tool, which returns a model-summarized rendering of the Clerk XML rather than raw bytes. Party totals from each fetch were compared with the totals already recorded in al-votes.json for the same roll, and all 28 matched.",
  "Several XML reads were cut off partway through the alphabetical roll (after Steube/Strong/Stutzman/Suozzi/Sykes/Swalwell/Takano). Every Arizona member (Ansari, Biggs, Ciscomani, Crane, Gosar, Grijalva, Hamadeh, Schweikert, Stanton) sorts before every cutoff, and each read returned all Arizona members serving at the time: 9 in the 118th; 9 in early 2025; 8 on 2025-102 through 2025-203 while AZ-07 was vacant; 9 from roll 2025-285.",
  "The Clerk XML records some votes as 'Aye'/'No' (recorded-vote form) rather than 'Yea'/'Nay'; they are normalized to Yea/Nay here, matching al-votes.json (rolls 2023-243, 2024-119, 2024-226, 2024-345, 2025-190, 2025-203, 2026-214).",
  "Not Voting entries were confirmed on the Clerk HTML pages: Gosar on 2024-102 (clerk.house.gov/Votes/2024102, 12 not voting); Stanton on 2024-119 (/Votes/2024119, 11 not voting); Gosar and Stanton on 2025-007 (/Votes/20257). The record gives no reasons.",
  "Unusual votes also confirmed on HTML pages: Biggs was one of three Republicans voting No on H.R. 4763 (FIT21, 2024-226); Ansari was among the 45 Democrats voting Yea on H.R. 23 (ICC sanctions, 2025-007); Stanton voted Yea on S. 5 (Laken Riley Act, 2025-023).",
  "Andy Biggs is a candidate for governor (AZ-GOV), not AZ-05; his House record (AZ-05, 118th and 119th Congresses) is included under his name as it appears in az-races.json. In 119th-Congress XML he appears as 'Biggs (AZ)', distinct from 'Biggs (SC)'.",
  "Adelita Grijalva was sworn in Nov 12, 2025, the day of roll 2025-285, on which the Clerk records her Nay (confirmed at clerk.house.gov/Votes/2025285). She has no entries for earlier votes. 'Grijalva' entries on 118th-Congress rolls and on 2025-007/2025-023 are her father, Rep. Raúl Grijalva (died Mar 13, 2025), and are not included.",
  "Ansari and Hamadeh took office Jan 3, 2025, so they have no 118th-Congress entries. No other candidate on the Arizona ballot has served in the House. Jay Feely, Mark Lamb, Amish Shah, Jonathan Nez and the rest have no House record. David Schweikert (AZ-01) is not on the November ballot and is not included.",
  "Roll 2024-102 is H.Res. 1102 (concurring in the Senate amendment to H.R. 2882). Roll 2025-203 is H.Res. 590 (the rule that cleared the H.R. 4 rescissions package). Roll 2025-320 is recorded in the XML under S. 1071, the vehicle for the FY2026 NDAA, as keyvotes.json describes.",
  "party_majority and urls are copied from al-votes.json for the same ids; no new vote ids were needed."
 ]
